est-reference\" />"},"1103":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/overview-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/overview#for-the-integrator","content":"<Card title=\"Troubleshooting\" description=\"Distinguish transport, policy, issuance and installation failures.\" href=\"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/troubleshooting\" />"},"1104":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/overview-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/overview#contract-version","content":"This block describes `main` code inspected at commit `8f42c47157f9a36bac3ed5caa3692aebebe19c4b`. The site catalog publishes `main (unstable)`; this behavior is not attributed to a stable release. Before using another version, check its contract, particularly independent re-enrollment authentication. Client checks and live-instance tests are distinguished in the revision plan."},"1105":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/overview-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/overview#contract-version","content":"Gateway, TLS, provider and service configuration belongs to Deployment. Identity use in AWS or other destinations belongs to Integrations."},"1106":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/provisioning-strategies","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/provisioning-strategies","type":"page","content":"Provisioning strategies","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","IoT Fleets","Devices and identities","Enrollment with PKI"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/iot-fleets/enrollment/provisioning-strategies"},"1107":{"id"