ew/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","content":"You will issue an end-entity certificate for `device-001` using browser key and CSR generation. The result is `device.crt`, `device.key` and the issuing root's public certificate, `ca.pem`."},"2507":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"An active root CA with an available signing key and permission to issue. If one does not exist yet, follow Create your first CA."},"2508":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"Its public certificate in `ca.pem`; this example uses the root created in the previous path."},"2509":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"OpenSSL 3.x and a working directory with restricted access."},"2510":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"A client identifier: here we use `device-001`."},"2511":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#before-you-begin","content":"In this flow, the client's key is generated in the browser and must be downloaded when issuance finishes. If you lose it, you must generate a key and issue another certificate. The certificate inventory lets you download the public certificate, but cannot recover this key."},"2512":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#start-the-issuance","content":"Open the CA from the previous path, go to **Issued Certificates** and select **Issue New**."},"2513":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#choose-the-method","content":"Select **Generate Key & CSR in Browser** to follow this example."},"2514":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#choose-the-method","content":"If the key must be generated and kept on the destination system, use **Upload Existing CSR**, described in the authorities guide."},"2515":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#identify-the-certificate","content":"Enter `device-001` as the `Common Name`. Add subject details required by your policy and SANs if the consumer uses them to identify the client."},"2516":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#identify-the-certificate","content":"If you continue with manual registration, the `Device ID` will be exactly `device-001`."},"2517":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#configure-key-and-uses","content":"Choose an algorithm and size allowed by the profile; for example, ECDSA P-256 if permitted. For this client certificate, select **Digital Signature** and **Client Authentication**, and issue it as an end-entity certificate."},"2518":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#configure-key-and-uses","content":"Request, for example, 30 days of validity, always within the CA's lifetime. Review the issuance profile if the resulting content differs from the request."},"2519":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#issue-and-download","content":"Confirm issuance. Save the PEM certificate as `device.crt` and the private key as `device.key` in your prepared directory."},"2520":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-result","content":"Check in **Issued Certificates** that the certificate appears active. Note its serial number and verify the downloaded material using the checks below."},"2521":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#inspect-content-and-dates","content":"Check `CN=device-001`, the expected issuer, current validity, **Digital Signature** and the extended usage **TLS Web Client Authentication**. It must be an end-entity certificate: it must not declare `CA:TRUE` or enable **Certificate Sign**. If **Basic Constraints** is present, it must indicate `CA:FALSE`. If you requested SANs, check that the expected identifiers appear in the certificate."},"2522":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-chain","content":"The expected result is `device.crt: OK`. This check uses your explicit root and evaluates the chain, dates and compatibility with the TLS client purpose. Also check for the expected usages and names through the inspection above."},"2523":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate#verify-the-chain","content":"If you use an intermediate CA, the trusted root must be in `ca.pem` and you must supply the intermediates with `-untrusted intermediates.pem`. This variant is covered in the trust model."},"2524