fy** in KMS; check provider permissions and availability."},"2590":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"CSR"},"2591":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Correct PEM and verifiable signature."},"2592":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"`openssl req -in request.csr -noout -verify -text`."},"2593":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Profile"},"2594":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Selected source, existing ID, allowed algorithm and size."},"2595":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Check Profiles precedence; CA and DMS resolve differently."},"2596":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Result"},"2597":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Appropriate subject, SAN, usages and dates."},"2598":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"Compare CSR, profile and certificate; successful issuance does not establish consumer acceptance."},"2599":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"For unexpected certificate fields, review `Honor Subject`, `Honor Key Usage`, `Honor Extended Key Usages` and `Honor Extensions`. The latter preserves SAN only, without validating entitlement to those names. Validity is not automatically clamped to CA expiration."},"2600":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#issuance-fails","content":"For CA reissuance failures, check revocation and date: reissuance is not supported for a revoked or already expired CA. To change its key, use Hierarchy and rotation."},"2601":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"Check each boundary independently:"},"2602":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**Record:** read the correct certificate again by serial and issuer. Confirm status, reason and time; expired or permanently revoked records reject further transitions."},"2603":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**Endpoint:** inspect AIA and CDP. Query those URLs from the consumer’s network; an old route or incorrect issuer can explain a discrepancy."},"2604":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**OCSP:** save a fresh response, verify signature and timestamps, and observe status. An HTTP error for an absent serial does not mean `Good` or guarantee a signed `Unknown`."},"2605":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**CRL:** compare `latest_crl`, number and timestamps with the downloaded list. Check the serial in its contents. If unchanged, review `regenerate_on_revoke`, event delivery, jobs, signing and storage with the deployment operator."},"2606":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"**Client:** check cache, policy for expired or unavailable evidence, critical IDP extension and rejection of a new connection."},"2607":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#ocsp-or-crl-do-not-reflect-a-change","content":"Reactivation from `CertificateHold` needs a new CRL for the client to stop seeing the hold. Reactivating a CA does not restore its descendant cascade; inspect every status and individual operation failure."},"2608":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#the-chain-validates-but-the-connection-fails","content":"Check expected identity, SAN, KU/EKU, matching key, presented intermediates and consumer permissions. Distinguish server TLS trust, client authentication and action authorization. Follow Validation for positive and rejection tests."},"2609":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/platform/pki/troubleshooting#the-chain-validates-but-the-connection-fails","content":"When escalating a problem, provide identifiers, error and relevant public evidence, including query timestamps and version. This distinguishes issuance, publication and consumer application failures."},"2610":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","type":"page","content":"Security","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security"},"2611":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","content":"How to report a security vulnerability in Lamassu privately, what to include in a report and which releases receive security fixes."},"2612":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"Report a vulnerability"},"2613":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#what-to-include-in-a-report","content":"What to include in a report"},"2614":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#supported-versions","content":"Supported versions"},"2615":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#responsible-disclosure","content":"Responsible disclosure"},"2616":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","content":"Found a security vulnerability in lamassuiot, lamassu-dashboard, or lamassu-helm? This page explains how to report it privately, what to include in your report and which releases receive security fixes."},"2617":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"Do not report security vulnerabilities through public GitHub issues, discussions, or pull requests. Public reports disclose the problem before maintainers can fix it."},"2618":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"Instead, report privately using GitHub Security Advisories for the affected repository:"},"2619":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"lamassuiot"},"2620":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"lamassu-dashboard"},"2621":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"lamassu-helm"},"2622":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"This lets maintainers assess and address the issue before it is publicly disclosed."},"2623":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#report-a-vulnerability","content":"If private vulnerability reporting is not enabled for that repository, report the vulnerability privately to lamassuiot\\@lksnext.com before disclosing any details publicly."},"2624":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#what-to-include-in-a-report","content":"Describe the vulnerability, its potential impact, and steps to reproduce it using non-sensitive, redacted examples."},"2625":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#what-to-include-in-a-report","content":"Do not include in the report:"},"2626":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security#what-to-include-in-a-report","content":"Credentials, tokens, or private keys"},"2627":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/security-16","page_i