ion/pkcs8`"],[2183,"`ARCHIVED` settings of a deleted CA can be deleted, with `DELETE` or from the console's Verification Authorities page. That CRL stops being served — anyone checking its certificates against it will no longer find it — while the CRLs already published remain in the bucket. The action cannot be undone."],[934,"`auth_mode`"],[2800,"`auth.oidc.apiGateway.jwks`, `auth.authorization.rolesClaim` and `auth.authorization.roles.admin` are removed with no compatibility aliases, and the schema rejects them. Their settings move into `services.authz`: the JWKS URL becomes `services.authz.jwkUrl`, and the role claim and administrator role become a claim rule of the bootstrap principal. `auth.oidc.frontend` is unchanged."],[541,"`authz` extracts the credential and resolves all active principals matching it."],[561,"`authz` gathers the entity rules of the granted policies."],[2887,"`authz` is the authorization service's own storage for principals, grants and policies. `pki` is the database the authorization engine queries when it evaluates policies against entities. Only the `database` field of each entry is read; the connection always uses the global `postgres.hostname`, `postgres.port`, `postgres.username` and `postgres.password` values. Each schema can also supply its own username and password through the `LAMASSU_AUTHZ_CREDENTIALS_<SCHEMA>_USERNAME` and `LAMASSU_AUTHZ_CREDENTIALS_<SCHEMA>_PASSWORD` environment variables, which take precedence over the global `postgres.username` and `postgres.password` values when set. See Credential environment variables."],[544,"`authz` looks for an HTTP rule granting that action."],[622,"`authz` validates every token against `services.authz.jwkUrl`, which is fetched from the `authz` pod. The Gateway does not validate tokens itself: Lamassu services authorize each request through `authz`, and routes labeled `auth=external`, such as the Job Manager ones, are checked by the Gateway through `authz` when `auth.externalAuthorization` is enabled. The endpoint must serve the keys of the issuer configured in `auth.oidc.frontend.authority`."],[1288,"`auto` mode"],[1451,"`auto` mode delegates full device provisioning in AWS to Lamassu at enrollment time. When the device successfully completes its EST enrollment and Lamassu emits the `EventBindDeviceIdentityKey` event, the connector automatically executes the following sequence:"],[1351,"`aws_config.access_key_id`"],[1347,"`aws_config.auth_method`"],[1367,"`aws_config.endpoint_url`"],[1343,"`aws_config.region`"],[1363,"`aws_config.role_arn`"],[1355,"`aws_config.secret_access_key`"],[1359,"`aws_config.session_token`"],[1873,"`C`: two-letter ISO 3166-1 country code."],[1383,"`ca_client`"],[2155,"`ca_id`"],[587,"`ca_trust.identity_type` accepts `fingerprint` or `authority_key_id`. In both cases you must provide the CA certificate in `ca_trust.pem`; Lamassu verifies both the signature and the expected identity of the CA."],[1500,"`certificateHold`"],[1822,"`CertificateHold` allows reactivating the parent while it is not expired, but does not restore child CAs or certificates permanently revoked during the cascade. Holding a CA therefore does not provide a reversible pause for its entire branch."],[940,"`CLIENT_CERTIFICATE_AND_EXTERNAL_WEBHOOK`"],[936,"`CLIENT_CERTIFICATE`"],[1634,"`CLIENT_CERTIFICATE`, configured in the independent re-enrollment block."],[1632,"`CLIENT_CERTIFICATE`; Validation CAs includes the direct bootstrap issuer; no expired certificates."],[584,"`cn_and_ca`: an exact or wildcard Common Name and a specific CA;"],[597,"`column_filters` applies conditions to columns the schema has declared filterable. All filters of the same rule are combined with AND."],[961,"`config.apikey_options`"],[957,"`config.auth_mode`"],[969,"`config.call_timeout`"],[967,"`config.insecure_skip_verify`"],[963,"`config.jwt_options`"],[959,"`config.log_level`"],[965,"`config.mtls_options`"],[1339,"`connector_id`"],[578,"`contains`, to check membership in a list or the presence of text in a scalar value."],[1199,"`Content-Type: application/pkcs10`, Base64 of DER, valid signature and a body preserved without double encoding."],[988,"`critical_delta`"],[2849,"`crl_options.subject_key_id_signer` is replaced by the required `crl_options.signer_serial_number`, the serial number of the existing certificate that signs the CRL. A new CA's initial value is the serial number of its current certificate. Requests that still carry `subject_key_id_signer` return an error. The authorization entity that holds these settings is also renamed; see CRL settings keyed by CA ID."],[2239,"`crl_options.subject_key_id_signer` was replaced by `crl_options.signer_serial_number`, which is required."],[2163,"`crl_options` field"],[882,"`csr` is **base64 of PEM**, unlike the EST body, which is base64 of DER. `http_request` contains URL and first header entries from available HTTP context. This body does not include an `operation` field; distinguish enroll and reenroll through the path and configured policy."],[553,"`default_action` requires at least one `base_paths` entry, and base paths are absolute paths such as `/api/wfx/nbi/v1`."],[2221,"`DELETE`"],[136,"`dev.lamassu.io`"],[1218,"`device not preregistered`"],[1379,"`device_manager_client`"],[1711,"`device-001` appears in inventory with the expected DMS."],[594,"`direct_grants` limits the rule to concrete identifiers. The value `*` covers all instances of the type. A superadministrator policy uses wildcards in schema, entity, actions and grants; a least-privilege policy should avoid them whenever possible."],[1375,"`dms_manager_client`"],[990,"`enable_expired_renewal`"],[926,"`enable_replaceable_enrollment`"],[922,"`enrollment_ca`"],[577,"`equals`, for exact equality;"],[928,"`est_rfc7030_settings.auth_mode`"],[992,"`est_rfc7030_settings.client_certificate_settings.validation_cas`"],[1626,"`EST_RFC7030` / `JITP`."],[921,"`EST_RFC7030` for these operations."],[1407,"`EventBindDeviceIdentityKey`"],[