ide key generation** switch and a **Key type** selection: `ECDSA` P-256, P-384 or P-521, or `RSA` with 2048, 3072 or 4096 bits; the defaults are P-256 for `ECDSA` and 4096 bit for `RSA`. Algorithm and size come from its `key` field, stored as `{type,bits}` where P-256, P-384 and P-521 map to `bits` 256, 384 and 521; `key` is omitted when disabled. The profile must permit them. The response contains an unencrypted PKCS#8 key inside TLS alongside the certificate. See format and extraction in EST reference."],[1936,"`Sign as CA` sets `IsCA` and the basic constraints needed for an authority. Lamassu enforces this: a profile with `Sign as CA` is consumed only when creating or reissuing a CA. Any signing request that resolves to such a profile is rejected — direct signing with a CA, including certificate issuance requests on it, and DMS enrollment or re-enrollment. Nothing validates the profile when it is saved: if a CA's default profile or a DMS profile has `Sign as CA` enabled, the problem appears on the first signing request that resolves to it — for a DMS profile, when a device tries to enroll or re-enroll — and renewal stays blocked until the profile is changed."],[2175,"`signer_serial_number`"],[1175,"`simplereenroll` rejects the revoked current certificate. Investigate the reason and prepare an authorized readmission procedure; do not disable authentication to force it."],[110,"`ssh-keygen` only when using `--with-hsm`"],[1874,"`ST`: state or province."],[2157,"`status`"],[1371,"`subscriber_event_bus`"],[616,"`SUPER ADMIN`, which grants all actions over the `authz` and `pki` domains."],[301,"`tls.certManagerOptions.certSpec.addresses` adds IP subject alternative names to the TLS certificate."],[2804,"`toolbox` is renamed to `connectivityTest`, and the `helm test` hook uses the upstream `curlimages/curl` image pinned by digest."],[2174,"`true`."],[1466,"`Unconfigured` → `None` / `Auto`"],[1204,"`unexpected status code: <n>: redirects are not followed`"],[2393,"`Unknown` if the certificate and issuer can be retrieved."],[951,"`url`"],[2870,"`va.role.update` becomes `va.crl-settings.update` and `va.role.crl.init` becomes `va.crl-settings.init`; `va.role.crl.create` keeps its name and its payload. Every subject changes from `crl/<ski>` to `crl/<ca-id>`, and the payload of the renamed events changes from the old VA role to the CRL settings of the CA, with `ca_id` instead of `ca_ski`. The alerts migration renames the event types of existing subscriptions automatically, but it does not rewrite their conditions — JSON Path, JSON Schema or JavaScript: review conditions that filter on the old payload or on the old `crl/<ski>` subject, including those for `va.role.crl.create`. Direct event-bus consumers and audit searches must adopt the new names and payload themselves."],[2828,"`validate_server_cert`"],[2166,"`validity`"],[2798,"`values.schema.json` rejects unknown keys, so every block that 4.0.0 removed or renamed — `toolbox`, `auth.oidc.apiGateway`, `auth.authorization` and others — fails `helm lint` and `helm upgrade` outright. Step 2 lists every change."],[924,"`verify_csr_signature`"],[1208,"`webhook config must not reference files`"],[1212,"`webhook mTLS certificate and key are invalid: …`"],[1206,"`webhook response exceeds 1048576 bytes`"],[107,"`yq`"],[2558,"<Card title=\"1. Create your first CA\" description=\"Create an evaluation root and save its public certificate as ca.pem.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/create-certificate-authority\" />"],[2559,"<Card title=\"2. Issue and verify a certificate\" description=\"Issue for device-001 and check content, chain and key correspondence.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/issue-certificate\" />"],[2950,"<Card title=\"Access control\" description=\"Principals, policies and the first administrator.\" href=\"/docs/platform/administration/access-control\" />"],[2453,"<Card title=\"Apply PKI to devices\" description=\"Associate certificates with inventory and prepare enroll