,[72,"Unlimited"],[64,"Up to 1,000"],[68,"Up to 10,000"],[2240,"Update the client to send the new field."],[1817,"Update the enrollment CA and profile of the DMSs. While old-CA cohorts still renew, add the previous enrollment CA to each DMS's re-enrollment validation CAs (`reenrollment_settings.est_rfc7030_settings.client_certificate_settings.validation_cas`): the new enrollment CA is trusted automatically, but the old one was the enrollment CA and appears in no re-enrollment trust list, so without that entry its certificates can no longer renew. The DMS guide documents the setting."],[2779,"Update the values file"],[1974,"Updating a profile affects future issuances; it does not modify already-signed certificates. Test changes before applying them to a CA in production and keep the operational justification."],[210,"Upgrading Lamassu"],[1195,"URL, clock, server SAN and approved root in `est-trust.pem`. Resolve trust in Deployment; do not skip verification."],[2034,"Use **Quick Inspect** for a quick review or **View Details** for subject, SAN, usages, chain, dates and metadata."],[588,"Use `any_from_ca` only when every identity issued by that CA should share the same permissions. If a CA issues certificates for different populations, separate access by serial or CN, or use different issuing CAs."],[173,"Use a different local SoftHSM chart"],[336,"Use a front-door SNI design only when the internal Gateways must retain independent TLS or mTLS policy:"],[1842,"Use a key from the KMS"],[625,"Use a second user without the role and confirm the same operation is denied. This test catches misread claims, overly broad policies and accidental `failOpen` configurations."],[2470,"Use an evaluation instance or an authority intended for these tests. The example creates a root that issues directly; to design an operational hierarchy, see Hierarchy and rotation."],[155,"Use an unpacked local Lamassu chart"],[2062,"Use and monitoring"],[1767,"Use audit logs to investigate changes and