es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#sincronización-del-estado-del-certificado","content":"Sincronización del estado del certificado"},"1295":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#estados-del-certificado","content":"Estados del certificado"},"1296":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#desconexión-forzada-al-revocar","content":"Desconexión forzada al revocar"},"1297":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#device-shadow-y-automatización","content":"Device Shadow y automatización"},"1298":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#qué-escribe-el-conector-en-el-shadow","content":"Qué escribe el conector en el shadow"},"1299":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#políticas-de-aws-iot","content":"Políticas de AWS IoT"},"1300":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#solución-de-problemas","content":"Solución de problemas"},"1301":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","content":"La integración de Lamassu con AWS IoT Core cubre el puente entre la PKI gestionada por Lamassu y la plataforma de conectividad de AWS. Cuando un dispositivo obtiene su certificado a través del proceso de enrolamiento EST, el conector se encarga de que ese certificado y la identidad asociada sean reconocidos en AWS IoT Core sin intervención manual. El resultado es que el dispositivo puede autenticarse directamente en AWS con el mismo certificado X.509 que Lamassu emitió."},"1302":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","content":"Desde el punto de vista del protocolo, el dispositivo se autentica ante AWS IoT Core mediante TLS mutuo (mTLS): presenta su certificado X.509 emitido por Lamassu como certificado de cliente, y AWS IoT Core verifica la cadena de certificados hasta llegar a la CA registrada en la cuenta. Lamassu actúa como autoridad de certificación (CA); el conector se encarga de que esa CA esté registrada en AWS y de que el certificado del dispositivo sea conocido por la plataforma antes de que el dispositivo intente conectarse (en modo `auto`) o en su primera conexión (en modo JITP)."},"1303":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","content":"Este documento está dirigido tanto al administrador PKI, que necesita configurar el conector y registrar las CAs, como al desarrollador de firmware de dispositivos, que necesita entender cómo se nombran los Things, cómo funciona el Device Shadow y qué ocurre cuando un certificado se revoca. Para el desarrollador de firmware, el dato más importante es que el **nombre del Thing en AWS (ThingName) corresponde siempre al Common Name (CN) del certificado emitido por Lamassu**, independientemente del modo de aprovisionamiento."},"1304":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#arquitectura-del-conector","content":"El conector de AWS IoT Core es un proceso Go independiente, un binario o contenedor separado del núcleo de Lamassu. En un despliegue monolítico se compila por defecto (etiqueta de compilación `!noaws`) y se activa mediante `aws_iot_manager.enabled: true` en el fichero de configuración. En despliegues distribuidos, se ejecuta como un contenedor propio con acceso a los servicios de CA, DMS Manager y Device Manager de Lamassu a través de HTTP."},"1305":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#arquitectura-del-conector","content":"El conector no sondea los servicios de Lamassu periódicamente. En su lugar, **se suscribe al bus de eventos interno** de Lamassu (AMQP o AWS SQS/SNS, configurable) y reacciona a los eventos que le interesan: creación o actualización de CAs, creación o actualización de DMS, vinculación de identidad de dispositivo, cambio de estado de certificado, actualización de metadatos de certificado y actualización de metadatos de dispositivo. Este modelo orientado a eventos garantiza que la sincronización con AWS sea casi inmediata y no genere carga de sondeo."},"1306":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#arquitectura-del-conector","content":"Para evitar bucles infinitos, el conector ignora cualquier evento cuyo campo `source` de CloudEvent coincida con su propia URI de origen. Esto previene que las escrituras de metadatos que el propio conector realiza vuelvan a disparar el mismo flujo."},"1307":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#arquitectura-del-conector","content":"Cuando se ejecutan varios conectores en paralelo, por ejemplo, para distintas cuentas de AWS, cada instancia tiene su propio `connector_id`. Todos los metadatos que el conector escribe en Lamassu se almacenan bajo la clave `lamassu.io/iot/{connector_id}`, lo que permite coexistencia sin colisiones."},"1308":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#prerrequisitos","content":"Antes de activar el conector es necesario disponer de una cuenta AWS con los permisos IAM adecuados y tener el conector correctamente configurado. El proceso de despliegue (Docker Compose, Kubernetes o binario) se describe en la documentación de despliegue."},"1309":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#permisos-iam-necesarios","content":"La identidad IAM con la que opera el conector debe tener al mínimo los siguientes permisos sobre los recursos de la cuenta destino:"},"1310":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#permisos-iam-necesarios","content":"Acción IAM"},"1311":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#permisos-iam-necesarios","content":"Propósito"},"1312":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#permisos-iam-necesarios","content":"`iot:GetRegistrationCode`"},"1313":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#permisos-iam-necesarios","content":"Obtener el código de verificación para el registro de CA en Primary Account"},"1314":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#permisos-iam-necesarios","content":"`iot:RegisterCACertificate`"},"1315":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#permisos-iam-necesarios","content":"Registrar la CA en AWS IoT"},"1316":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#permisos-iam-necesarios","content":"`iot:DescribeCACertificate`"},"1317":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#permisos-iam-necesarios","content":"Consultar el estado del registro de la CA"},"1318":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#permisos-iam-necesarios","content":"`iot:CreateThing` / `iot:UpdateThing`"},"1319":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-68/es/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws